From 6a8ff7c670aaf8b86ed9444595369a9d0750a2f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:12:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(skills): review fork prompt names skills whose replayed
 copy is stale [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Long-lived sessions load a skill once (e.g. kanban-orchestrator), and other
sessions' reviews edit it later. Each later review of that session replays
the old copy, patches from it, and read-before-write refuses (correctly) with
'content has not been loaded in this review turn' — one failed call per
review before the fork re-views (coach: kanban-orchestrator, 2bde8f).

Read seeding already compares every replayed skill_view against the live
file; it now also reports the mismatches, and the review prompt lists them:
'these skills changed on disk ... call skill_view before any write'. The fork
re-views first instead of being refused. The guard itself is unchanged.
---
